.TH MEMEX-SEARCH 1 "August 2026" "memex 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memex-search \- search memex archives with PCRE2 patterns
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memex search
.RI [ -i ]
.RI [ -w ]
.RI [ -F ]
.RI [ -m " N]"
.RI [ --format " FMT]"
.I PATTERN
.RI [ ARCHIVE ]
.PP
.B memex search
.RI [ -i ]
.RI [ -w ]
.RI [ -F ]
.RI [ -m " N]"
.RI [ --format " FMT]"
.B --service
.I FOLDER
.B --account
.I NAME
.I PATTERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B memex search
searches mmap archives under
.BR ~/memex .
With no
.BR --service ,
no
.BR --account ,
and no archive path, the search is systemwide: every
.B *.majestic
under
.B $HOME/memex ,
leftover
.B *.archive
when there is no sibling same-stem
.BR .majestic .
Open maps the
.B .majestic
file with
.B PROT_READ
and
.BR MAP_SHARED .
That is a virtual mapping of the file, not a heap allocation of the file size.
Search reads that map. It does not copy the text blob into a
.BR Vec .
RSS is the pages the CPU has faulted, not the file size at mmap. The intended
page for text is 2 MiB. New ingest pads so text starts at a 2 MiB file offset.
A systemwide search maps all listed archives, holds those maps, compiles PCRE2
once, then runs PCRE2 on each packed span of already-mapped text with min(file
count, available parallelism) workers. AND requires both words in the same
title or the same message, not anywhere in the archive. Search does not call
.B MADV_DONTNEED
after every archive while the search is still running. Hits are unique
(conversation id, field, and the entire packed span text). After uniqueness,
identical packed bodies print once, then occurrence rows list archive path,
conversation id, and field. Two conversation ids or two archives with the
same sentence are one snippet and two occurrence rows. Two different bodies
stay two snippet blocks. One packed message is one hit even when PCRE2
matches it many times. Duplicate packed copies of the same body in one
conversation print once. Default print cap is 100 snippet groups.
It does not walk
.B $HOME
for live export dumps. Ingest owns discovery. It does not mmap
.BR .zst .
It does not spawn
.BR rg .
.PP
Search uses mmap text, grep-searcher, and grep-pcre2 only. A pattern that is
not slash-wrapped is a human query. Slash-wrapped
.B /regex/flags
is PCRE2 (the same engine as
.BR "rg -P" ).
There is no PCRE1 and no rust-regex fallback. After mapping, search logs
.B searching N archives
on stderr, then one compact line per worker completion. It clones the PCRE2
matcher per worker so match-data is not shared.
.PP
.B --service
and
.B --account
together, or an explicit archive path, search one file and do not scan home.
.PP
Durable search flags may be set in
.I ~/.config/majestic/memex.toml
under
.B [search]
.RI ( ignore_case ,
.IR fixed_strings ,
.IR word_regexp ,
.IR max_count ,
.IR format ,
.IR archive ).
A missing file uses crate defaults (flags false, max_count 100, format human, archive unset). CLI flags
override the file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -i ", " --ignore-case
Case insensitive (Unicode).
.TP
.BR -w ", " --word-regexp
Whole word. Without
.BR -w ,
a match may sit inside a stored word.
.TP
.BR -F ", " --fixed-strings
Phrase or literal string.
.TP
.BR -m " N" ", " --max-count " N"
Unique messages printed per archive. Default 100. 0 means no cap.
.TP
.BI --format " human|json|toon"
Stdout report encoding. Default
.BR human
(grouped snippets and occurrence rows).
.B json
and
.B toon
use the same hit objects as MCP (a hits array of snippet groups and occurrences).
Status (searching N archives, then searching k/N path and a running unique-hit count) goes to stderr. Do not print one line per match.
.TP
.BI --service " FOLDER"
Folder under
.B $HOME/memex
(for example
.BR agents/grok ).
.TP
.BI --account " NAME"
Username file stem.
.SH SEARCH PATTERNS
.nf
Want                 Pattern
OR                   lizard OR catfooding  or  lizard|catfooding
AND, any order       lizard AND the
                     (bare words are implicit AND)
Phrase               "hello world"  or  -F 'hello world'
Case insensitive     -i  or  /Catfooding/i
Whole word           -w
Regex                /<regex>/  flags: i, g, m, s, x
PCRE2 AND            /(?=.*lizard)(?=.*the)/
.fi
.PP
A pattern that is not slash-wrapped is a human query. A single-quoted shell
string is just that query. Bare words join with implicit AND (lookaheads, any
order). AND requires both words in the same packed span (one title or one
message). It does not mean both words appear anywhere in the archive. AND and
OR are case-insensitive keywords.
.B |
is OR. Double quotes mark a contiguous phrase. Metacharacters in bare words
and phrases are escaped.
.B -i
is case insensitive.
.B -w
is whole word.
.B -F
is a phrase or literal and skips human and slash compile.
.B /pattern/i
is PCRE2 with case insensitive.
.B g
means all matches; search already unique-hits by message.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
memex search 'lizard OR catfooding'
memex search 'lizard AND the'
memex search '"hello world"'
memex search '/Catfooding/i'
memex search -F 'hello world'
memex search -i catfooding
memex search -w food
memex search --format json 'lizard AND the'
memex search --service agents/grok --account personal PATTERN
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR memex (1)
